      "value": "If D=0, choose x₀∈E by H001. Projection F→I is onto and 1-Lipschitz. Mapping covers by this map cannot increase diameters, so dim_H(I)≤dim_H(F). Since I has nonempty interior in ℝ, the pinned interval dimension theorem gives dim_H(I)=1. Thus dim_H(F)≥1=D+1. For n=0, this branch handles the only possible E⊆ℝ⁰: E is a singleton and D=0, so no positive-diameter replacement is needed. Combine with the upper bound for n≥1."
